2026.10.10: v0.34.0
    QPCC extensions: _Get_tag/_Tag_of are renamed _Static_tag/_Dynamic_tag
    (one is a compile-time discriminator for a named member, the other reads
    the stored runtime tag); _Function_pointer writes a function pointer type
    in prefix form (_Function_pointer int (int, char *) a; -- the return type
    and parameter list come first) and, bare, is the storage type for any
    function pointer from N3914: convertible to and from every function
    pointer type and void *, not callable without a cast, and still distinct
    from a real function pointer type in _Generic; _Lambda(a, &b) T (params)
    { body } closures with by-value and by-reference captures plus
    _Closure_environment, lowered to a { fn, env } pair whose environment
    holds the captures in the enclosing frame (escaping is undefined
    behaviour); `void x = f();` evaluates the call and declares nothing; new
    hand-written headers taggedunion.h, function_pointer.h and lambda.h; the
    oracle grows to 155 fixtures

2026.10.10: v0.35.0
    QPCC gains `qpcc run`: it drives clang for the preprocessing (`clang -E -P`,
    with the hand-written headers on the include path) and the linking, so an
    ordinary C file can be compiled and executed in one step; it forwards the
    program's exit status, passes -I/-D/-U through to the preprocessor,
    forwards everything after -- to the program, and reports missing clang
    clearly. The driver's errors now name the original source file rather than
    the temporary preprocessed one and exit 1 without a panic trace. New FFI:
    `mbt_native_exit`. Calls to a function with no declaration in scope now
    warn, because such a call to a variadic callee has to use the vararg ABI
    and cannot be inferred (implicit declarations stay accepted for the
    non-variadic libc helpers the self-host build relies on). The oracle grows
    to 158 checks
